# Benchmarking papers

```
Jorge, E., Foissac, S., Neuvial, P., Zytnicki, M., & Vialaneix, N. (2025). A comprehensive review and benchmark of differential analysis tools for Hi-C data. Briefings in Bioinformatics, 26(2), bbaf074.

Zheng, Y., Zhou, P., & Keleş, S. (2021). FreeHi-C spike-in simulations for benchmarking differential chromatin interaction detection. Methods, 189, 3-11.

```

# Tools references


```
diffHiC:

Lun ATL, Smyth GK (2015). “diffHic: a Bioconductor package to detect differential genomic interactions in Hi-C data.” BMC Bioinformatics, 16, 258.

[diffHiC](https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/diffHic.html)

```

```
HiCcompare:

Stansfield JC, Cresswell KG, Vladimirov VI, Dozmorov MG (2018). “HiCcompare: an R-package for joint normalization and comparison of HI-C datasets.” BMC Bioinformatics, 19(1). doi:10.1186/s12859-018-2288-x, https://github.com/dozmorovlab/HiCcompare.

[HiCcompare](https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/HiCcompare.html)

```

```
multiHiCcompare:

Stansfield JC, Cresswell KG, Dozmorov MG (2019). “multiHiCcompare: joint normalization and comparative analysis of complex Hi-C experiments.” Bioinformatics, 35(17). doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btz048, https://github.com/dozmorovlab/multiHiCcompare.

[multiHiCcompare](https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/multiHiCcompare.html)
```

# Generate environment

```bash
mamba env create -f ../environment_benchmarking.yml
```

# Benchmarking execution - Spikes
```bash
# inside benchmarking

hic_path=$(realpath "../test_data/GM12878-HRC.hic")
chromosomes=$(seq 1 22)
resolutions=(10000 50000 100000 250000 500000)
pval=(0.01)
k_spikes=(2 3 4)


for resolution in ${resolutions[@]}; do
    for chromosome in ${chromosomes[@]};do
        for p_val in ${pval[@]}; do
            for k in ${k_spikes[@]}; do
                sbatch --job-name=Benchmarking_DifFraction_spikes_chr${chromosome}_res${resolution} \
                    run_benchmarking_spikes.sh \
                    -f ${hic_path} -c ${chromosome} -r ${resolution} -k ${k} -p ${p_val}
            done
        done
    done
done

```

# Benchmarking execution - Downsample
```bash

hic_path=$(realpath "../test_data/GM12878-HRC.hic")
chromosomes=$(seq 1 23)
resolutions=(10000)
pval=(0.01)

ds=(0.1 0.25 0.5 0.75 1.0)

for resolution in ${resolutions[@]}; do
    for chromosome in ${chromosomes[@]};do
        for p_val in ${pval[@]}; do
            for d in ${ds[@]}; do
                sbatch --job-name=ds_Benchmarking_DifFracTion_chr${chromosome}_res${resolution}_ds${d} \
                    run_benchmarking_downsample.sh \
                    -f ${hic_path} -c ${chromosome} -r ${resolution} -d ${d} -p ${p_val}
            done
        done
    done
done

```

# Benchmarking execution - Downsample and spikes
```bash

hic_path=$(realpath "../test_data/GM12878-HRC.hic")
chromosomes=$(seq 1 22)
resolutions=(50000 10000 100000 250000)

pval=(0.01)

ds=(0.1 0.25 0.5 0.75 1.0)
k_spikes=(2 3 4)

for resolution in ${resolutions[@]}; do
    for chromosome in ${chromosomes[@]};do
        for p_val in ${pval[@]}; do
            for d in ${ds[@]}; do
                for k in ${k_spikes[@]}; do
                    sbatch --job-name=ds_Benchmarking_DifFracTion_chr${chromosome}_res${resolution}_ds${d}_k${k} \
                        run_benchmarking_downsample_n_spikes.sh \
                        -f ${hic_path} -c ${chromosome} -r ${resolution} -d ${d} -p ${p_val} -k ${k}
                done
            done
        done
    done
done

```